```php
function extractDivClassNames($htmlContent) {
    $classNames = [];
    $dom = new DOMDocument();
    $dom->loadHTML($htmlContent);
    $divs = $dom->getElementsByTagName('div');

    foreach ($divs as $div) {
        if ($div->hasAttribute('class')) {
            $classAttr = $div->getAttribute('class');
            $classArr = explode(' ', $classAttr);
            foreach ($classArr as $class) {
                if (!in_array($class, $classNames)) {
                    $classNames[] = $class;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return $classNames;
}
```

This solution uses the `DOMDocument` class in PHP to parse the HTML content and extract the class names from the `div` elements. It iterates through each `div` element, checks for the presence of the `class` attribute, and then extracts and stores the unique class names in an array. Finally, it returns the array of unique class names found in the `div` elements.

