public static bool CustomTryParse<TEnum>(string value, out TEnum result) where TEnum : struct
{
    if (!typeof(TEnum).IsEnum)
    {
        throw new ArgumentException("TEnum must be an enumerated type");
    }

    result = default(TEnum);
    foreach (var enumValue in Enum.GetValues(typeof(TEnum)))
    {
        if (string.Equals(enumValue.ToString(), value, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            result = (TEnum)enumValue;
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

In the solution, the `CustomTryParse` method first checks if the generic type `TEnum` is an enum type. It then iterates through all the enum values using `Enum.GetValues` and compares each value with the input string using a case-insensitive comparison. If a match is found, the corresponding enum value is assigned to the `result` parameter, and the method returns `true`. If no match is found, the method returns `false`, and the `result` parameter is set to the default value of the enum type.

