print(custom_base_arithmetics(20, 33, 2, "diff"))    # "0b11010"
print(custom_base_arithmetics(20, 33, 8, "average")) # "0o32"
```
In this implementation, the function first checks if the base and the range of numbers (n through m) are valid. If not, it returns -1. The function also supports lowercase and uppercase operation strings.

