The above depreciation notice is displayed after upgrading to PHP 8.1 relating to the code below:
`enter code here`

public function next() {
    $this->fetch();
    return next( $this->data );
}


Can supress this by adding #[\ReturnTypeWillChange] but would rather solve / change the code without using the above method.
Any ideas on how we can change this code to be PHP 8.1 + compatible. ?

In PHP 8.1, methods that implement certain interfaces now need to specify the explicit return type. If the interfaces happen to be one from either `\Iterator`, `\ArrayAccess`, `\Serializable`, `\Stringable`, the `next()` method should return `void`:

```php
public function next(): void {
    $this->fetch();
    next($this->data);
}
```
But please note that the `next()` function itself does not actually return any value, it simply moves the internal pointer of an array. So, suppose you expect this function to retrieve the next element after moving the pointer, you need to call the `current()` function on `$this->data` later in your code. 

If `next()` here is an implementation of the `\Iterator` method, then you would not expect any output as per the PHP documentation, hence explicitly declaring the return type as `void` is the correct way to fix your issue.

