The reason you're seeing this error is because your lambda expression is using `return`, but since your expression type is `Action`, your method cannot return a value. `Action` delegate types are intended for methods that do not return a value (void methods).

You can fix this by just calling `methodCall.Compile().Invoke(m);` without trying to return the result. Here is your modified function:

```
private Expression<Action<T>> GenerateMethodCallWithMoniroting<T>(string recurringJobId, Expression<Action<T>> methodCall)
{
    return m =>
    {
       var transaction = Agent.Tracer.StartTransaction(recurringJobId, ApiConstants.ActionExec);
       try
       {
           methodCall.Compile().Invoke(m);
       }
       finally
       {
           transaction?.End();
       }
    };
}
```

In this modification, your `try` block executes the action `methodCall.Compile().Invoke(m);` without trying to return any result, which is in line with the specification of `Action<T>`. If a `Transaction` occurs, it is handled in the `finally` block.

