Here's a Java program implementing the Bubble Sort algorithm with Multithreading:

```java
class BubbleSort implements Runnable{

    private int[] array;
    public Thread thread;
    public int[] sortedArray;

    public BubbleSort(int[] array){
        this.array = array;
        this.thread = new Thread(this);
        this.thread.start();
    }

    @Override
    public void run(){
        this.sortedArray = bubbleSort(this.array);
    }

    private int[] bubbleSort(int[] array){
        for(int i = 0; i < array.length-1; i++){
            for(int j = 0; j < array.length-i-1; j++){
                if(array[j] > array[j+1]){
                    int temp = array[j];
                    array[j] = array[j+1];
                    array[j+1] = temp;
                }
            }
        }
        return array;
    }
}

class MergeArrays{

    public static int[] merge(int[] firstArray, int[] secondArray){
        int[] mergedArray = new int[firstArray.length + secondArray.length];

        int i=0, j=0;
        while(i+j < mergedArray.length){
            if(i == firstArray.length || (j<secondArray.length && firstArray[i] >= secondArray[j])){
                mergedArray[i+j] = secondArray[j++];
            } else {
                mergedArray[i+j] = firstArray[i++];
            }
        }
        return mergedArray;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
        int[] array = {5, 2, 8, 10, 4, 9};

        int[] firstHalf = new int[array.length/2];
        int[] secondHalf = new int[array.length - array.length/2];

        System.arraycopy(array, 0, firstHalf, 0, firstHalf.length);
        System.arraycopy(array, firstHalf.length, secondHalf, 0, secondHalf.length);

        BubbleSort bs1 = new BubbleSort(firstHalf);
        BubbleSort bs2 = new BubbleSort(secondHalf);

        bs1.thread.join();
        bs2.thread.join();

        int[] sortedArray = MergeArrays.merge(bs1.sortedArray, bs2.sortedArray);

        for(int i : sortedArray){
            System.out.print(i + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

This program splits the given array into two halves. Each half is sorted by an independent thread using BubbleSort. When both threads complete their sorting, their results are merged using the MergeArrays class. Note that the `main` method waits for both threads to complete sorting using `join` before proceeding to merge the sorted halves.

