```bash
npx create-react-app interactive-grid
```

Once done, navigate into the new folder:

```bash
cd interactive-grid
```

Step 2: Install Required Packages

In this case, we're going to use `styled-components` for styling. Install it using:

```bash
npm install styled-components
```

Step 3: Create a new Grid component

In `/src` directory, create a new component called `Grid.js` and add this code:

```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import styled from 'styled-components';

const Grid = () => {
  const [selectedCells, setSelectedCells] = useState([]);
  const grid = Array(5).fill(Array(5).fill(0)); // Creates a 5x5 grid

  const handleCellClick = (i, j) => {
    setSelectedCells([...selectedCells, { i, j }]);
  };

  return (
    <Wrapper>
      {grid.map((row, i) => (
        <div key={i}>
          {row.map((cell, j) => {
            const isSelected = selectedCells.some(
              (cell) => cell.i === i && cell.j === j
            );

            return (
              <Cell
                key={j}
                isSelected={isSelected}
                onClick={() => handleCellClick(i, j)}
              />
            );
          })}
        </div>
      ))}
    </Wrapper>
  );
};

const Wrapper = styled.div`
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
`;

const Cell = styled.div`
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  margin: 5px;
  background-color: ${(props) => (props.isSelected ? 'blue' : 'grey')};
`;

export default Grid;
```

In this code, a React function component `Grid` is created. It uses `useState` to keep track of the selected cells. The component renders a grid of cells, which are grey by default. When clicked, they turn blue.

Notice the `styled-components` usage, making it easy to apply styles in a modular way.

Step 4: Usage of the Grid component

Replace the content in `App.js` with the following:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import Grid from './Grid';

const App = () => {
  return (
    <div className="App">
      <header className="App-header">
        <div>
          <p>Interactive Grid</p>
        </div>
        <Grid />
      </header>
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
```

Step 5: Start the application:

Run the following command to start the application:

```bash
npm start
```

The command runs the application in development mode. Open `http://localhost:3000` to view it in the browser.

Remember, this is a simple demonstration and doesn't handle mouse position color change. To achieve such functionality, you may need to use mouse event attributes and change the cell color accordingly. It's also worthy to note that depending on the size of the grid, you may need to optimize how state is being updated to avoid performance issues.

